  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <p>Near the hilltop village of Mons, in the Var, the Pont de Mons is a river spot on the Siagnole. No official source specifies the rule for dogs or for swimming here.</p>

      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A still fairly little-known swimming spot on the Siagnole, below the hilltop village of Mons (according to unofficial descriptions of the place). The Siagnole, or Siagne de Mons, is a roughly 5.8 km tributary of the Siagne that rises at Mons (Pays de Fayence tourist office).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Parking is very limited (about 3 spaces, according to unofficial descriptions) on the side of the road to Mons; a path then leads down to the Pont de Mons. If it is full, the area around the Pont de Siagne, a little further on, is described as an alternative.</p>
      <p>As for the rules: the Pays de Fayence tourist office's dog-travel guide (May 2025) states that, unless banned by a municipal bylaw shown on signs, river banks and watercourses allow dogs to swim, and it cites the Siagne among the rivers where they can cool off. It does not cite this specific site. A prefectoral order of 26 July 2026 also placed the upper Siagne zone, including Mons, on drought alert (the Siagnole partly supplies drinking water to the Pays de Fayence).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: arrive early to get a parking space, keep your dog on a leash, and call the Mons town hall (04 94 39 22 39) to find out the exact rule before letting him swim.</div>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>Are dogs allowed at the Pont de Mons?</h3>
      <p>No official source specifies it for this spot. The Pays de Fayence dog-travel guide states that, unless a municipal bylaw is posted, dogs can swim in the rivers of the area; ask the town hall or check the signs.</p>
      <h3>Where to park to reach the Pont de Mons?</h3>
      <p>Parking is very limited, about 3 spaces according to unofficial descriptions, on the side of the road to Mons.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Mons, perched at over 800 m altitude, offers a superb view of the Siagnole gorges from the access road via the RD 563 (Pays de Fayence tourist office).</p>
